$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: template-website/winning-trimming-com-au/header-footer
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-06"
summary: >-
  Global Header and Footer managed via Payload globals. Header has navItems array (max 12, link
  fields with no appearances) and revalidates on change. Footer is a 4-column server component: (1)
  Brand with logo, ABN, and serving-area description, (2) Visit & Contact with address and a
  prominent green phone CTA button (Call 1300 799 882), (3) Hours (7am-3pm Mon-Fri, Sat by
  appointment, Sun closed), (4) Quick Links with curated in-code links to About, Our Work, Get a
  Quote, Blog, My Account. Admin-managed supplementary links from the Footer global render below
  Quick Links when present. Both globals revalidate on change. anyone read access.
$system: template-website/system
$service: template-website/winning-trimming-com-au
intent: >-
  Let staff manage site navigation and footer links through the Payload admin panel without code
  changes, with automatic revalidation when links are updated.
status: built
implementation:
  primary: src/Header/config.ts
  test_code: ""
  test_code_status: none
see_also:
  - template-website/winning-trimming-com-au/shared-fields
flows:
  - id: update-nav
    name: Update navigation
    description: Staff edit header or footer nav items in admin.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: navigate
        target: Payload admin globals header or footer
      - id: s2
        action: set
        target: navItems array with link fields (label, url, type)
      - id: s3
        action: save
        target: afterChange hook fires revalidateHeader or revalidateFooter
      - id: s4
        action: revalidate
        target: site navigation refreshed on next page load
contracts:
  - id: globals
    description: Header and Footer are Payload globals, not collections
    must_have:
      - "Header: GlobalConfig slug header"
      - "Footer: GlobalConfig slug footer"
      - Both registered in payload.config.ts globals array
  - id: public-read
    description: Anyone can read header and footer globals
    must_have:
      - read returns true on both
  - id: nav-items
    description: navItems array of link fields
    must_have:
      - Header navItems max 12, link with appearances false
      - Footer navItems max 6, link with appearances false
  - id: revalidation
    description: afterChange hooks revalidate on save
    must_have:
      - Header afterChange revalidateHeader hook
      - Footer afterChange revalidateFooter hook
tests:
  - id: public-read-header
    setup:
      auth: none
      global: header
    expect:
      - result: navItems readable
  - id: max-rows-header
    setup:
      navItems: 13
    expect:
      - result: maxRows 12 enforced
decisions:
  - id: globals-over-collection
    decision: Use Payload globals rather than a singleton collection
    rationale: >-
      Globals are designed for single-instance site config (nav, footer). No slug, no versions,
      simpler admin UX than a singleton collection.
    date: "2026-09-06"
  - id: link-no-appearances
    decision: Nav links use appearances false (plain links, no button styling)
    rationale: Nav items are text links, not CTA buttons. Disabling appearances keeps the admin UI clean.
    date: "2026-09-06"
  - date: "2026-09-06"
    decision: Curate the 4 footer columns in code rather than the Footer global
    id: curated-footer-columns
    rationale: >-
      Footer links must stay in sync with actual routes (/about, /our-work, /quote, /posts,
      /account). Managing these in a Payload global risks broken links when routes change. The
      Footer global is retained for admin-managed supplementary links that render below Quick Links.
  - date: "2026-09-06"
    decision: Add a prominent green phone CTA button in the footer contact column
    id: footer-phone-cta
    rationale: >-
      The phone number is the primary conversion action for a service business. A styled CTA button
      (bg #607A00, brand green) draws the eye more than a plain text link. Includes a phone emoji
      and Same-day quotes over the phone subtext.
  - date: "2026-09-06"
    decision: Update hours to 7am-3pm Mon-Fri, Saturday by appointment, Sunday closed
    id: hours-update-2026-09
    rationale: >-
      Corrected from the previous 8am-4pm and 8am-Midday. Applies to both the site footer
      (Footer/Component.tsx) and the email footer (utilities/email.ts) so they stay consistent.
